    //- 1st Details Row
  .container-fluid
    #detailSection1.row.promo-row
      .col-md-6
        h2 Increase student engagement
        img(src="/assets/images/promo/value-prop__thoughts.png")
      .col-md-6
        p.sub Engagement is the #1 reason teachers love Edji. It’s simple: students have more fun and learn more when they can have input.
        p Edji brings easy engagement to lessons you already have. Your students will love learning on Edji, because their thoughts are seen by you and their peers in a collaborative, social environment.
        p Students have thoughts, and want to share them. Edji increases student engagement by bringing peer-to-peer collaboration to any lesson.
    //- 2nd Details Row
    #detailSection2.row.promo-row.promo-row--accent
      .col-md-8
        h2 Personalize education on-the-go
        .row
          .col-md-6
            p.sub You need feedback to personalize education. Edji is your real-time window into student thoughts, helping you identify where students are performing well, and where a student needs an assist.
          .col-md-6
            p Without real time data on student thoughts, you’ll always be one step behind on what students are thinking.
            p Edji is your real-time, hands-off window into student thoughts, helping you identify where students are performing well, and where a student needs an assist.
      .col-md-4
        img(src="/assets/images/promo/value-prop__fastest.png")
    //- 3rd Details Row
    #detailSection3.row.promo-row
      .col-md-4
        h2 Annotate PDFs Collaboratively
        p.sub Educational content—textbooks, scans, supplementary materials—is often stuck in a PDF format. Free it with Edji.
      .col-md-4
        img(src="/assets/images/promo/value-prop__annotate.png")
      .col-md-4
        p Edji brings collaborative word highlighting to PDFs. Teachers can upload scanned pages for their students, and interact with the text digitally, as if typed.
        p Edji has integrated collaborative highlighting allowing a whole class to interact with the same text at the same time — together.
